  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request Path",
      "items": [
        "CertificateExtractionService is the hub: it owns the extractor and the parser and returns CertificateDetails",
        "The controller is thin — it delegates and wraps the result in ExtractionResponse",
        "CertificateDetails shows 4 of its 7 components; the others are certificateName, issuer and issueDate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Error Path",
      "items": [
        "ApiException carries an HttpStatus and a machine code; it is the only failure type the app throws deliberately",
        "GlobalExceptionHandler converts it into ApiErrorResponse, whose nested ErrorDetail holds just the code",
        "ApiErrorResponse.ErrorDetail is a nested record and is shown by name rather than as its own box"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two Processes",
      "items": [
        "CertificateCli shares the JAR but runs as its own process and talks HTTP to the server",
        "It has no compile-time link to the controller — the only wiring between them is the JSON contract",
        "PDFBox and Tesseract are third-party libraries, so they are not types in this graph"
      ]
    }
  ]
